      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَحَدَهُمَا ( عليهما السلام ) عَنِ الْإِمَامِ يَضْمَنُ صَلَاةَ الْقَوْمِ قَالَ لَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Hadeed, from Jameel, from Zurara who said, ",
          "‘I asked one of the two (5<sup>th</sup> or 6<sup>th</sup> Imam<sup>asws</sup> about the Imam being responsible for a <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> of the people’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Ali ibn Hadid from Jamil ibn Darraj from Zurarah who has said the following: “I once asked one of the two Imam, ‘Alayhim al-Salam, if the Imam is responsible for Salah (prayer) of the people. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, he is not responsible.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
